# Sound controllers stay powered (#228). On 2026-10-02 the A9 lost all sound
# until a restart: the HDMI audio controller (0000:c6:00.1) had refused to go
# from D0 to D3hot ("Refused to change power state", 66 times since
# 2026-09-19), and once that left its output carrying only zeros. Keeping the
# controller out of runtime power management stops it ever trying. An idle
# sound chip saves next to nothing on a console plugged into a television.
# Every HD-audio controller (PCI class 0x0403xx), so any machine's HDMI or
# analog one. tuned's [audio] timeout is the codec's power saving, not this,
# and is left alone.
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="pci", ATTR{class}=="0x0403*", ATTR{power/control}="on"
